<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Kraken (applied by scripts/sign.sh).

  Code-integrity exceptions (com.apple.security.cs.*): NONE.
    - allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory: Kraken has no JIT. wgpu talks to
      Metal, whose shader compilation happens in a system service, not in our process.
    - disable-library-validation: Kraken links only system frameworks and loads no
      third-party plug-ins or dylibs, so library validation never trips.
    - allow-dyld-environment-variables: not needed. The hardened runtime makes dyld
      ignore DYLD_* for the Kraken process itself. Shells started inside Kraken are
      separate binaries with their own signatures, and DYLD_* exported from a user's
      shell rc files keeps working for them; only DYLD_* set when *launching* Kraken
      is dropped, which is the point of the hardened runtime.
    - Child processes do NOT inherit these entitlements (or the hardened runtime);
      each program the terminal spawns runs under its own signature.

  Resource-access entitlements (NOT exceptions to code integrity):
    TCC attributes programs launched from a terminal to the terminal app (the
    "responsible process"). Under the hardened runtime, a protected resource whose
    entitlement is missing is denied silently, without ever prompting the user. So a
    user running `osascript`, `ffmpeg -f avfoundation`, `imagesnap`, etc. inside
    Kraken would just get failures. Terminal.app and iTerm2 carry these for the
    same reason. Each one still requires the user to approve the prompt (the
    matching NS*UsageDescription strings are set in Info.plist by bundle.sh).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Apple Events: `osascript -e 'tell application "Finder" ...'`, `open -a` scripting. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
  <true/>
  <!-- Microphone: CLI audio tools (sox/ffmpeg recording, speech-to-text CLIs). -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
  <!-- Camera: CLI capture tools (imagesnap, ffmpeg avfoundation input). -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
  <true/>
  <!--
    Deliberately not included (add with a matching NS*UsageDescription if users need them):
    com.apple.security.personal-information.location / .addressbook / .calendars /
    .photos-library.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
